// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b3
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b3.1" source="b3" target="SNOMED_CT:43914001" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3 SNOMED CT 286367001 43914001 = the ICF chapter-3 root combining TWO distinct function
        domains: voice functions (b310, phonation/laryngeal) and speech functions (b320, articulated
        spoken language), plus fluency/rhythm (b330) and pre-lingual vocal functions. No single SNOMED CT
        standard concept spans both voice AND speech; the source is a multi-component chapter. Per the
        multi-target rule, emit one partial target per axis. (1) SNOMED CT 4184650 (sctid 43914001) =,
        active, covers the voice/phonation axis. (2) SNOMED CT 4118706 (sctid 286367001) =, active, covers
        the speech axis. Each captures one aspect (partial); the active SNOMED CT 286367001 43914001
        7787002 is retired (invalid=D) so 286367001 is the active speech-capability observable. Weak
        tier per partial-without-companion-cap on each axis: the chapter is a heterogeneous grouping,
        and each target covers only one of its components.
        """
}
mapping "b3.2" source="b3" target="SNOMED_CT:286367001" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
}
mapping "b310.1" source="b310" target="SNOMED_CT:43914001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b310 SNOMED CT 43914001 = ICF b310 Voice functions: the body functions of producing sound
        through the larynx (phonation), including production, quality, pitch, loudness, resonance.
        Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT observable that captures
        voice-as-a-laryngeal-function and is the closest standard equivalent of ICF b310; it sits under
        the voice/observable hierarchy alongside 30976009, 52583008, 44523003. Broader rather than exact
        only because ICF b310 is a multi-child function block (b3100 production, b3101 quality, b3102
        pitch, b3103 loudness, b3104 resonance) where the SNOMED CT concept is a single flat observable,
        and SNOMED CT does not separately name as a grouping. High tier : direct term-and-scope match
        (laryngeal voice function = voice functions) verified active in the mirror, but no independent
        Athena crosswalk re-verified, and one-level-broader in model granularity.
        """
}
mapping "b3100.1" source="b3100" target="SNOMED_CT:363917000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3100 SNOMED CT 363917000 = ICF b3100: the specific voice sub-function of PRODUCTION of
        voice (the act of generating voice sound via laryngeal phonation — onset, continuity,
        coordination of phonation). Target =, active. This is the only SNOMED CT observable that names
        voice production as such; sibling concepts (228144006, 289186000) are finding/impairment
        concepts, not the production function. Broader rather than exact: 363917000 denotes the
        *characteristic* of the type of voice production (a quality/feature observable), which is one
        axis of the broader ICF b3100 production function; the target fully contains the production
        domain but models it as a characteristic rather than as the production function itself. Low tier
        : the closest defensible voice-production observable, term-verified active, but the SNOMED CT
        concept is a framing that does not fully denote the ICF production function, and there is no
        independent crosswalk. (286325005 considered and rejected: it is a capability/assessment
        observable, one step further from the production function than 363917000.)
        """
}
mapping "b3101.1" source="b3101" target="SNOMED_CT:286343009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3101 SNOMED CT 286343009 = ICF b3101: the voice sub-function of voice QUALITY (the
        timbre/texture/features of the produced voice, distinct from pitch/loudness). Target =, active.
        This is the only SNOMED CT observable that names voice quality as a function/capability; the
        adjacent findings (289188004, 56505000, 76412005) are specific quality findings, not the quality
        function. Broader: 286343009 frames voice quality as an (capability assessment) where ICF b3101
        frames it as the function itself; the target fully subsumes the source domain. Moderate tier :
        best-available defensible voice-quality observable, term-verified active, but the framing is one
        level of granularity away from the ICF, and no independent crosswalk.
        """
}
assessment "b3108.omop" source="b3108" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b3109.omop" source="b3109" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b320.1" source="b320" target="SNOMED_CT:286259006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b320 SNOMED CT 286259006 = ICF b320 Articulation functions: the body functions of
        coordinating laryngeal, oral, nasal and respiratory structures to produce speech sounds
        (articulation), including b3200 articulation of phonemes, b3201 articulation of words, etc.
        Target =, active RF2 production. This is the direct SNOMED CT observable capturing
        articulation-as-a-function/capability and is the closest standard equivalent of ICF b320; it
        sits under a rich articulation-observable hierarchy (286260001 place, 286264005 manner,
        286274008 words, 286293005 clearly). Broader rather than exact only because ICF b320 frames and
        SNOMED CT frames (a capability framing), and ICF b320 is a multi-child block where the SNOMED CT
        concept is a single observable. High tier : direct term-and-scope match (ability to articulate =
        articulation functions), verified active, but the capability framing plus block-vs-single
        granularity makes it one-level-broader with no independent crosswalk. (The legacy 53026004 is
        inactive/D; 286259006 is its active successor family.)
        """
}
mapping "b330.1" source="b330" target="SNOMED_CT:35622009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b330 SNOMED CT 35622009 = ICF b330 Fluency and rhythm of speech functions: the chapter-level
        grouping covering b3300 fluency, b3301 rhythm, b3302 rate, b3303 melody (a multi-child block
        anchor spanning fluency AND rhythm AND rate AND melody/prosody). No single SNOMED CT observable
        spans all four sub-functions; the only defensible single standard target that subsumes the whole
        block is the broader prosody observable. Target =, active. Prosody (the combination of rhythm,
        rate, stress, intonation/melody in speech) is the nearest standard ancestor that fully contains
        the fluency-and-rhythm-of-speech block: rhythm, rate and melody are all components of prosody,
        and fluency is its clinical correlate. Broader: a deep broader climb (the target covers the
        rhythm/rate/melody axis and overlaps fluency, but is the nearest ancestor that contains the
        block). Low tier : clinically defensible ancestor but loose (multi-hop, the block bundles four
        sub-functions each of which has its own tighter SNOMED CT observable — 363921007, 37129003,
        1197010003 Rate — and no independent crosswalk).
        """
}
mapping "b3300.1" source="b3300" target="SNOMED_CT:363921007" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3300 SNOMED CT 363921007 = ICF b3300 Fluency of speech: the speech sub-function of
        producing smooth, continuous, appropriately-paced speech without interruption (the fluency
        function, clinically the function whose impairment is stuttering/cluttering). Target =, active
        RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (fluency of speech as a speech
        function), confirmed by literal FSN term match in the mirror. The SNOMED CT concept is the direct
        functional observable where 289196009 and 39423001 are its finding/impairment correlates.
        exact_match: same concept, term-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b3301.1" source="b3301" target="SNOMED_CT:37129003" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3301 SNOMED CT 37129003 = ICF b3301 Speech rhythm: the speech sub-function of the rhythmic
        patterning of speech (the temporal pattern of stress and timing between syllables/words). Target
        =, active RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (speech rhythm as a
        speech function), confirmed by literal FSN term match. The SNOMED CT concept is the direct
        functional observable where 82883008 is its impairment correlate. exact_match: same concept,
        term-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b3302.1" source="b3302" target="SNOMED_CT:1197010003" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3302 SNOMED CT 1197010003 = ICF b3302 Speed/rate of speech: the speech sub-function of the
        speed (words/min) at which speech is produced. Target =, active RF2 production (sctid
        1197010003, a post-2018 SNOMED CT International concept). Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical
        concept (rate of speech as a function), confirmed by literal FSN term match; ICF = speech
        speed/rate = SNOMED CT. The SNOMED CT concept is the direct functional observable where
        690461000220106 and 690471000220100 are its valued findings. exact_match: same concept,
        term-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b3303.1" source="b3303" target="SNOMED_CT:35622009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3303 SNOMED CT 35622009 = ICF b3303 Melody of speech (speech prosody/melody): the speech
        sub-function of the melodic/intonational contour of speech (variation in pitch/stress over an
        utterance = the melodic aspect of prosody). Target =, active RF2 production. No dedicated /
        observable exists in SNOMED CT (the mirror has no or observable entity); prosody is the nearest
        standard ancestor and fully contains the melody-of-speech function (melody/intonation is a
        primary component of prosody). Broader: prosody is a true ancestor (melody ⊂ prosody) but also
        covers rhythm, rate, and stress, so it is one level broader than the melody-specific source.
        Moderate tier : best-available defensible ancestor, term-verified active, but the target is
        broader (covers rhythm/rate/stress too) and there is no independent crosswalk. (The deficit
        correlates 20937004, 112089001 are findings, not functions.)
        """
}
assessment "b3308.omop" source="b3308" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b3309.omop" source="b3309" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b340.1" source="b340" target="SNOMED_CT:75382007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b340 SNOMED CT 75382007 = ICF b340 Alternative vocalization functions: the chapter-level
        block covering b3400 production of tones (sustained phonation/singing-like tones) and b3401
        making a range of sounds (non-speech vocalization: humming, growling, sound-making beyond
        conventional speech). No single SNOMED CT observable spans both sub-functions exactly. Target =,
        active RF2 production. This is the only SNOMED CT observable that captures non-speech / alternative
        vocalization as a function (it sits in the vocalization hierarchy distinct from speech
        articulation and denotes vocalization beyond undifferentiated cry). Broader rather than exact:
        75382007 is a developmental-vocalization concept (the stage beyond reflexive cry, including
        sustained sounds and sound play) that overlaps but is not co-extensive with the ICF b340 (which
        is a lifelong functional category for non-speech voice use such as singing/humming/growling).
        Low tier : the only defensible non-speech-vocalization observable, term-verified active, but the
        SNOMED CT concept is developmental-vocalization-framed and only partially denotes the ICF concept;
        no independent crosswalk. The specific children b3400/b3401 each get their own tighter proposals
        below.
        """
}
mapping "b3400.1" source="b3400" target="SNOMED_CT:39140000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3400 SNOMED CT 39140000 = ICF b3400: the alternative-vocalization sub-function of
        PRODUCTION OF TONES (sustained vocal-tone production, e.g. singing a sustained note, humming a
        tone — the function of generating and sustaining pitched vocal tones). Target =, active RF2
        production. No dedicated / observable exists in SNOMED CT; the nearest standard observable that
        captures the pitched-tone-production domain is vocal pitch (the closest adjacent observables
        24220009, 5660006 are duration/volition aspects, not tone production). Broader: 39140000
        captures the pitch/tonal axis of tone production but does not denote the sustained-production
        function the ICF code specifies. Low tier : the closest defensible pitched-tone observable,
        term-verified active, but it is a pitch (frequency) characteristic rather than a production
        function, and there is no independent crosswalk; real doubt remains.
        """
}
mapping "b3401.1" source="b3401" target="SNOMED_CT:306753009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b3401 SNOMED CT 306753009 = ICF b3401: the alternative-vocalization sub-function of MAKING A
        RANGE OF SOUNDS (producing a variety/sequence of vocal sounds beyond speech — sound play,
        non-speech sound sequences, varied vocal sound-making). Target =, active RF2 production. No
        dedicated / observable exists in SNOMED CT; the nearest standard observable in the sound-production
        hierarchy is the ability to produce voiced sounds (sibling to 306757005 voiceless sounds,
        306761004 voice/voiceless combinations, 286349008 imitate vocalization). Broader: 306753009
        captures the production of voiced sounds as a capability but does not denote the specificity the
        ICF code makes (it is one axis of the broader b3401 function). Low tier : the closest defensible
        sound-production observable, term-verified active, but the SNOMED CT concept is a single-sound-type
        capability rather than the range/sequence function, and no independent crosswalk.
        """
}
assessment "b3408.omop" source="b3408" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b3409.omop" source="b3409" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b398.omop" source="b398" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b399.omop" source="b399" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
